querying apart from the basic 5 CRUD operations
-----------------------------------------------
1. Query method / finder methods
	- easy to create it
	- based on how the find method is created spring data jpa will create the sql query internally
2. using @Query
	 @Query("select u from User u where u.emailAddress = ?1")
		- @Query uses JPQL and not SQL
		- SQL works on the DB table name and column but JPQL works on Entity class and field name
3. using @NamedQuery
	- here the query is mentioned above the entity class
	- a name is given for the query and this name vam be used in the dao interface
	@Entity
	@NamedQuery(name = "User.findByEmailAddress",
  			query = "select u from User u where u.emailAddress = ?1")
	public class User {

	}
4. using @NativeQuery
	@NativeQuery("SELECT * FROM USERS WHERE EMAIL_ADDRESS = ?1")
  	Map<String, Object> findRawMapByEmail(String emailAddress); 
		here we use sql query



