WT Algorithm
--------------
generating JWT token
--------------------
1. upon successful authentication by authentication manager, generate JWT token
2. usually we can pass the user name and generate token
3. this is done in the /api/users/login endpoint


validating JWT token
--------------------

-----> request----->JwtFilterChain-------> /api/users (PUT)



JwtFilterChain algorithm
1. check if Authorization header is present
2. If not present, let the request reach the endpoint and return
3. If the Authorization header is present
	- Take out the value   (Bearer <jwt>)
	- Cut off the first 7 characters and keep the token in jwt variable
4. if the username is not null and security context does not have the authenticated information
	- fetch the complete user info by username
	- next validate the token by extracting all the claimns
	- if token is tampered, an exception is thrown
	- else return true
5. if token is valid
	- set the spring security context with the username and roles
6. pass the token to the intended endpoint
		

avoid updating another customer's profile by passing their id in path variable or request body
---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. Dont pass id in path variable or request body
2. instead from the jwt token extract the username
3. then fetch the user info from db by calling findByUserName()
4. then use the id from that fetched record to update the profile

